{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-blog-post-tsx","path":"/blog/2023-11-06--pulse-secure-systemd-resolved-and-chrome/","result":{"data":{"site":{"siteMetadata":{"disqus":"edward-j-schwartz"}},"post":{"htmlAst":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some days I hate computers.  Today is one of those days.  My work computer froze\nover the weekend (which is another long, frustrating story that I won't go into\nright now), so I had to reboot.  As usual, I logged into our Pulse Secure VPN,\nand opened up Chrome.  And Chrome can't resolve anything.  I can't get to\nregular internet sites or intranet sites.  What the heck?"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"My first thought is that this is somehow proxy related.  But no, even when\ndisabling the proxy, I still can't resolve internal hostnames."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"But tools like "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"dig"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"ping"}]},{"type":"text","value":" work.  I open up Firefox, and that works too.\nOK, that's weird.  I open up "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"chrome://net-internals/#dns"}]},{"type":"text","value":" in Chrome and confirm\nthat it can't resolve anything.  I try flushing the cache, but that doesn't\nwork.  I try a few other things, like disabling DNS prefetching and safe\nbrowsing, but none of those help either."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I take a look at "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"/etc/resolv.conf"}]},{"type":"text","value":", which contains a VPN DNS server presumably\nadded by Pulse Secure, and "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"127.0.0.53"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"systemd-resolved"}]},{"type":"text","value":" resolver.  I\nconfirm that "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"resolvectl"}]},{"type":"text","value":" does "},{"type":"element","tagName":"em","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" know about the Pulse Secure DNS server.  I\nadd it manually with "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"resolvectl dns tun0 <server>"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and Chrome starts working\nagain.  OK, well that's good.  But how do we fix it permanently?"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This seems relevant: "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/17512"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PulseSecure VPN does not work with\nsystemd-resolved"}]},{"type":"text","value":".  Oh, maybe\nnot.  The \"fix\" is to publish documentation that the Pulse Secure developers\nshould read.  Sigh.  After reading more closely, I see something about the\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"resolvconf"}]},{"type":"text","value":" command, which they do already support.  I don't seem to have that\ncommand, but that is easily fixed by a "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"apt install resolvconf"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and I confirm\nthat after reconnecting to the VPN, "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"systemd-resolved"}]},{"type":"text","value":" knows of the VPN DNS\nservers.  And Chrome works.  Yay!"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"So what happened that this suddenly became a problem?  I'm not sure.  One\npossibility is that Chrome started ignoring "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"/etc/resolv.conf"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and directly\nusing "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"systemd-resolved"}]},{"type":"text","value":" if it appears to be available."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I really hate when my computer stops working, so I hope that if you are affected\nby this problem and find this blog post, it helps you out."}]}],"data":{"quirksMode":false}},"excerpt":"Some days I hate computers.  Today is one of those days.  My work computer froze\nover the weekend (which is another long, frustrating story…","timeToRead":1,"fields":{"slug":"/blog/2023-11-06--pulse-secure-systemd-resolved-and-chrome/"},"frontmatter":{"tags":["linux"],"author":{"jsonId":"Edward J. Schwartz","bio":"Computer Security Researcher","twitter":"@edmcman","avatar":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/4ed6d/ed.png","srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/4ed6d/ed.png 80w","sizes":"80px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/1deab/ed.webp 80w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"80px"}]},"width":80,"height":80}}}},"title":"Pulse Secure, systemd-resolved and Chrome","updatedDate":"Nov 6, 2023","image":null}},"recents":{"edges":[{"node":{"id":"dc140854-cd47-57bc-9923-4189a0ca61a6","fields":{"slug":"/blog/2025-07-11--quantifying-and-mitigating-the-impact-of-obfuscations-on-machine-learning-based-decompilation-improvement-published-at-dimva-2025/"},"timeToRead":1,"frontmatter":{"title":"\"Quantifying and Mitigating the Impact of Obfuscations on Machine-Learning-Based Decompilation Improvement\" Published at DIMVA 2025","image":null,"author":{"jsonId":"Edward J. Schwartz","avatar":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/8ef0e/ed.png","srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/8ef0e/ed.png 36w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/b0e74/ed.png 72w","sizes":"36px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/9a807/ed.webp 36w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/de323/ed.webp 72w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"36px"}]},"width":36,"height":36}}}}}}},{"node":{"id":"09105995-a671-52af-b503-961e210b7302","fields":{"slug":"/blog/2025-06-16--a-human-study-of-automatically-generated-decompiler-annotations-published-at-dsn-2025/"},"timeToRead":1,"frontmatter":{"title":"\"A Human Study of Automatically Generated Decompiler Annotations\" Published at DSN 2025","image":null,"author":{"jsonId":"Edward J. Schwartz","avatar":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/8ef0e/ed.png","srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/8ef0e/ed.png 36w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/b0e74/ed.png 72w","sizes":"36px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/9a807/ed.webp 36w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/de323/ed.webp 72w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"36px"}]},"width":36,"height":36}}}}}}},{"node":{"id":"abbe1ee2-919a-5f21-84b3-2886d2e0d960","fields":{"slug":"/blog/2025-05-02--re-compiling-ghidra-decompiler-output/"},"timeToRead":4,"frontmatter":{"title":"Re-compiling Decompiler Output","image":null,"author":{"jsonId":"Edward J. Schwartz","avatar":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/8ef0e/ed.png","srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/8ef0e/ed.png 36w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/b0e74/ed.png 72w","sizes":"36px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/9a807/ed.webp 36w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/de323/ed.webp 72w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"36px"}]},"width":36,"height":36}}}}}}},{"node":{"id":"bcb306e9-2fe5-5021-9fd1-7e03dae6739c","fields":{"slug":"/blog/2025-02-25--notes-neural-decompiler-artifacts/"},"timeToRead":2,"frontmatter":{"title":"Notes: Neural Decompiler Artifacts","image":null,"author":{"jsonId":"Edward J. Schwartz","avatar":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/8ef0e/ed.png","srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/8ef0e/ed.png 36w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/b0e74/ed.png 72w","sizes":"36px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/9a807/ed.webp 36w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/de323/ed.webp 72w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"36px"}]},"width":36,"height":36}}}}}}}]}},"pageContext":{"slug":"/blog/2023-11-06--pulse-secure-systemd-resolved-and-chrome/"}},"staticQueryHashes":[],"slicesMap":{}}